{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>כי העושק (for oppression).</b> He mentioned that it is good for the wise not to engage in matters of jest, and he mentioned that there is a thing that will turn him into a madman, and it is oppression. And something is missing before מתנה (gift), on account of ויאבד (and will destroy), a masculine form of speech, as in the verse ושונא מתנות יחיה (Proverbs 15:27), and like it: עד נמצא עולתה בך (Habakkuk 2:10)."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The comment is textually difficult: Ibn Ezra appears to argue that something has dropped out before מתנה, but the logic connecting ויאבד as masculine to the citation of Habakkuk 2:10 is obscure and possibly corrupt in the manuscript tradition; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:03.080840574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}